  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "indiscretion ( not exercising prudence and judgment ( in expen-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "diture, including charity, is evidently a better reading than",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "त्यागात् &c. where त्याग means ' liberality, giving away.' It",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "also keeps up symmetry. Fig, तुल्ययोगिता, विनश्यति indicating the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "common attribute.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 43. गतिः—passage out; money goet out in these three",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ways. यो &c.—The language here is rather condensed. वित्तं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "must be supplied from the first line as the object of ददाति and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "वित्तस्य after तस्य which means ' his ' answering to यः.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 44. शाणोल्लीढः—Cut or polished on a polishing stone. हेति-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "निहत—forcibly struck i. e. wounded with weapons. दलितः v. l.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "means ' shattered, hewn, and is a stronger term than निहतः.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "मदक्षीणः—मदेन क्षीणः Inst. Tat.; reduced by the flow of rut. Here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "क्षीणः has the same meaning as श्लक्ष्ण ( thin, which is a mark",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "of beauty ). This is preferable to क्षीणमदः which is a Bah. and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "implies the cessation of the flow of rut, and therefore the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "poet uses the rather unusual Inst. Tat. आश्यान०—श्यान from",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "श्यै to become dry or thick + क्तः shrunken. Cf. शनैः श्या-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "नीभूताः सितजलधरच्छेदपुलिनाः । + + + नभस्तः स्यन्दन्ते सरित इव",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "दीर्घा दशदिशः ॥ Mud. III. 7. As the floods subside in autumn",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "the rivers shrink back into their proper beds and look",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "beautiful with their pellucid water. Cf. वनस्पतीनां सरसां नदीनां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "तेजस्विनां कांतिभृतां दिशां च । निर्याय तस्याः स पुरः समन्ताच्छ्रियं दधानां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "शरदं ददर्श । Bhatti. II. 1. Also Rag. IV. 19. 21.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "कलाशेषः—( एका ) कला एव शेषो यस्य सः । Such a moon is con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "sidered not only beautiful but also an object of reverence. Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Rag V. 16. quoted in the Com. also प्रणमन्त्यनपायमुत्थितं प्रतिपच्चन्द्र-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "मिव प्रजा नृपम् । Kir. II. 11. For the poetical account of the wan-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ing of the moon, supposed to be drunk in turns by the gods,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "pitṛs &c., see our Raghu ( V. 16 ) and note thereon. तनिमन्—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "An abs. noun from तनु. The aff. इमनिच् ( इमन् ) is optionally",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "added, to form abstract nouns, to पृथु, मृदु, महत्, पटु, लघु &c. 'पृथ्वा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
